# 2FA setup checklist (frontend)

> Generated by `php artisan auth:setup --frontend-path=…` (the light-it auth package). It
> lists what the package could not do for you, because it never edits your files. Tick
> each box, then **delete this file**. How the screens work: `docs/google-2fa.md` in the
> package.

- [ ] **Install dependencies** (`{{ packageManager }}`): {{ dependencyReport }}
- [ ] **Use the 2FA-aware login hook** in `src/routes/(public)/_guest/login/-components/login-form.tsx`:
  1. Remove `import { useLogin } from "@/services/auth/actions";`
  2. Add `import { useTwoFactorLogin } from "../-hooks/use-two-factor-login";` right after
     `import { handleAxiosFieldErrors, redirectTarget } from "@/utils";`
  3. Replace `const loginMutation = useLogin();` with `const loginMutation = useTwoFactorLogin();`
- [ ] **Add the i18n keys** to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` (and translate them in `es.json`):
  `form.otp` and `form.recoveryCode` under `form`, and the `twoFactor` block at the top level.

Under `form`:

```json
"otp": "One-time code",
"recoveryCode": "Recovery code"
```

At the top level:

```json
"twoFactor": {
  "backToLogin": "Back to sign in",
  "verify": {
    "title": "Two-factor authentication",
    "oneTimePasswordDescription": "Enter the 6-digit code from your authenticator app.",
    "recoveryCodeDescription": "Enter one of the recovery codes you saved when you set up two-factor authentication.",
    "useRecoveryCode": "Use a recovery code instead",
    "useOneTimePassword": "Use your authenticator app instead",
    "submit": "Verify"
  },
  "setup": {
    "title": "Set up two-factor authentication",
    "loading": "Preparing your setup...",
    "loadError": "We couldn't start the setup. Sign in again to retry.",
    "scanQrCode": "Scan this QR code with your authenticator app.",
    "qrCodeAlt": "QR code for your authenticator app",
    "manualEntryKey": "Or enter this key manually:",
    "recoveryCodesTitle": "Recovery codes",
    "recoveryCodesDescription": "Save these codes somewhere safe. Each one signs you in once if you lose your device. They won't be shown again.",
    "copyRecoveryCodes": "Copy recovery codes",
    "recoveryCodesCopied": "Recovery codes copied",
    "recoveryCodesNotCopied": "Couldn't copy the recovery codes. Copy them by hand.",
    "confirmDescription": "Enter the 6-digit code from your authenticator app to finish."
  },
  "errors": {
    "invalidCode": "That code didn't work. Try again.",
    "tooManyAttempts": "Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.",
    "expired": "Your verification expired. Sign in again.",
    "unexpected": "Something went wrong. Try again in a moment."
  }
}
```

Check it worked: run `vite` once (`dev` or `build`) so the router adds the `/two-factor`
routes, then `{{ packageManager }} exec tsc --noEmit` passes and signing in with a 2FA
user asks for the code.
